{
  "name": "Angled sensor mount",
  "note": "A base with a ramp at 52 degrees on one end and a rib with a 3 degree draft on the other. A counterbored hole goes straight down into the ramp, where the face rises more than the counterbore's radius across it, so the counterbore's top has to clear the face well past where the axis meets it. A counterbore on the base reaches under the rib's foot, and has to leave the rib alone. A countersunk hole in the base and a tapped hole in the rib's top. The holes come down from a plane 100 above.",
